========================================================================
9. CURRENT RISKS AND LIMITATIONS
========================================================================

Persistence:
- backend/src/config/db.js explicitly reports mode "json-seed".
- There is no MongoDB/PostgreSQL/file adapter.
- All mutations disappear when the Node process exits.

Authentication:
- Demo passwords are stored as plain text in backend/src/data/users.js.
- AUTH_SECRET has a hard-coded development fallback.
- The custom token is HMAC-signed but is not a standard JWT.
- Login has no rate limiting or account lockout.
- Production must use hashed passwords, a strong external secret, HTTPS,
  rate limiting, and preferably a mature authentication library.

Authorization:
- Incident creation and status mutation are protected.
- Read endpoints and PDF downloads are public.
- Confirm whether environmental reports should be public before production.

Validation:
- requireFields checks only presence, not allowed values, ranges, or types.
- Latitude/longitude, severity, status, confidence, and hectares need schema
  validation before accepting untrusted production input.

PDF output:
- The PDF generator uses compact hand-built PDF syntax.
- Long descriptions do not wrap or paginate.
- Unicode and complex formatting support are limited.

Frontend data behavior:
- Report/history filtering is client-side after downloading all incidents.
- The Report dateRange state is displayed as a control but is not currently
  applied to filteredIncidents.
- The frontend does not currently expose login, incident creation, or status
  update flows, although the backend supports them.
- Live incidents are defined as the newest two items, not by an explicit
  active/resolved rule.

Operations:
- There is no request logger, structured application logging, health dependency
  check, automated backend test suite, or production deployment configuration.
- CORS permits one configured origin only, which is appropriate for local use
  but must be configured for each deployed frontend.

